userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A continuous signal is reconstructed from its samples by convolving the impulse train with a sinc kernel: every sample drops a scaled, shifted copy of the sinc, and the superposition of all copies is the reconstructed waveform.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Reconstruction is not guessing between samples — each sample simply contributes its own scaled sinc that is zero at every other sample, so the sum automatically threads through all samples and is the unique bandlimited signal behind them.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "A continuous signal is reconstructed from its samples by convolving the impulse train with a sinc kernel: every sample drops a scaled, shifted copy of the sinc, and the superposition of all copies is the reconstructed waveform.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
